---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Is this a fit? — KKT"
  description="We would rather tell you early if we are not the right partner. Here is how to tell — and where to look if it is not us yet."
  ogImage="/og/not-for-you.png"
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="prose-header">
        <div class="section-label">Honest fit</div>
        <h1 class="h1-page">When we are the right partner — and when we are not.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          We would rather tell you early that we are not the best fit than
          sell you an engagement that will not land. Here is how to tell —
          and where to look if it is not us yet.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose" data-reveal-stagger>
        <div class="rule">
          <div class="rule-num">01</div>
          <div>
            <h2>If you are earlier than ~$50M in revenue.</h2>
            <p>
              We are built for mid-sized retailers and fuel networks.
              Below that scale, our delivery model usually costs more
              than the value it can create for you — you would be
              paying for rigor you do not need yet. There are excellent
              partners sized for smaller companies, and starting with
              one of them is the right first move.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rule">
          <div class="rule-num">02</div>
          <div>
            <h2>If you want strategy without anyone shipping it.</h2>
            <p>
              Our work is shaped to put something operating into your
              business, not to produce a deck that sits on a shelf. If
              what you need right now is a slide-led strategy with no
              delivery team behind it, a strategy house will serve you
              better than we would.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rule">
          <div class="rule-num">03</div>
          <div>
            <h2>If there is no senior owner inside to inherit the work.</h2>
            <p>
              The systems we build keep running after we leave only if
              someone senior inside owns them — with real authority and
              real time, not just a title. If that person is not in
              place yet, the honest first step is to get them in seat,
              and we are glad to help you scope the role before we would
              start.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rule">
          <div class="rule-num">04</div>
          <div>
            <h2>If you need a model in production in four weeks.</h2>
            <p>
              We can run a diagnostic in four weeks. A model live in
              your business and moving real numbers in four weeks — that
              we cannot promise, and we would rather say so than
              over-commit. Good delivery has a floor on time, and we
              would happily walk you through a realistic one.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <blockquote class="rule-pull">
          <p>
            We would rather quote you a timeline that holds than one
            that sounds good in the room.
          </p>
        </blockquote>

        <div class="rule">
          <div class="rule-num">05</div>
          <div>
            <h2>If you are in heavily regulated banking, public sector, or defence.</h2>
            <p>
              These domains carry compliance bars and delivery patterns
              we do not claim deep expertise in. We respect that work
              enough not to pretend — firms built specifically for it
              will serve you better, and that is who we would point you
              toward.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rule">
          <div class="rule-num">06</div>
          <div>
            <h2>If the goal is just to &ldquo;deploy some AI&rdquo;.</h2>
            <p>
              If the ask is to deploy a chatbot, roll out Copilot, or
              run an LLM pilot with no business outcome attached, we are
              probably not your best call — we put data, models, and AI
              to work only where they earn their place against margin,
              cash, availability, customer value, or productivity. If
              there is a real outcome underneath the ask, though, let us
              talk about that instead.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rule">
          <div class="rule-num">07</div>
          <div>
            <h2>If you need a team to run things for you.</h2>
            <p>
              We work alongside your people and bring senior delivery
              rigor, AI capability, and PMO discipline — but we do not
              take over your operations, your IT department, or your
              data function. If what you need is full-service
              outsourcing or staff augmentation, a different kind of
              firm is the better fit.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <hr />

        <p class="methodology-link">
          The other half of this rigor — how we treat numbers when we
          do quote them — lives on <a href="/methods/cost-of-doing-nothing">/methods/cost-of-doing-nothing</a>.
          Public, dated, sourced.
        </p>

        <p class="closer">
          If you read all of this and still want to talk, that is usually a
          good sign.
        </p>

        <p class="cta-line">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Book a diagnostic</a>
        </p>

        <p class="advisor-nudge">
          Still not sure if you&rsquo;re on the right side of this list?
          <button type="button" class="advisor-inline" data-advisor-open>
            Ask the advisor →
          </button>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose-page {
    padding-top: clamp(40px, 6vh, 72px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(56px, 9vh, 96px);
  }
  .prose-header {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .section-label {
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .h1-page {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.5vw, 48px);
    line-height: 1.16;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    max-width: 22ch;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 20px);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 56ch;
  }

  .prose {
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .rule {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 56px 1fr;
    gap: 20px;
    margin: 36px 0;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .rule-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--accent-text);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    line-height: 1.4;
    padding-top: 4px;
  }
  .rule h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 26px);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
  .rule p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .rule-pull {
    margin: 48px 0;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    background: var(--surface-alt);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;
  }
  .rule-pull p {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.6vw, 26px);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 30ch;
  }
  .prose hr {
    margin: 40px 0 28px;
    border: none;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .prose .closer {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 20px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .prose .cta-line {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .methodology-link {
    margin: 28px 0 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .methodology-link a {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .methodology-link a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .advisor-nudge {
    margin-top: 32px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .advisor-inline {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
    font: inherit;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 500;
    cursor: pointer;
    margin-left: 6px;
  }
  .advisor-inline:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
